","account":"T2","old":"60–150s, ask 47–58¢, BRTI move ≥2bp, 10-minute trend ≥4bp, $5","new":"60–150s, ask 45–60¢, BRTI move ≥2bp, 10-minute trend ≥3bp, $5","reason":"Zero settled trades after ~9 hours. The 47–58¢ / 4bp-trend cousin almost never lined up live (T’s overlapping fill was 59¢ with a −2.5bp trend, which T2 would reject). Widening the ask to T’s 45–60¢ band and easing the trend floor from 4bp to 3bp is the smallest relaxation that stays clearly profitable on the 18-day first-hit backtest (~19 trades/day, +$58 after fees vs the original 13/day and +$130). The suggested 45–180s + 45–60¢ + 3bp combo backtested negative (−$61) and was not used. Time window and the 2bp BRTI-move threshold are unchanged."},{"time_pt":"6:36 PM PT Nov 10","account":"LFC","old":"A’s late favorite (ask ≥0.80, ≤50s left) + favorite ask continuously >0.55 for 90s + hard stop below 0.50, 5% equity","new":"A’s late favorite (ask ≥0.80) allowed from ≤70s left + favorite ask continuously >0.55 for 60s + hard stop below 0.50, 5% equity","reason":"The 90s confirm was not the main live blocker (0 filter_blocks; two late favorites held ~89s but could not fill into a one-sided late book). Shortening the confirm to 60s eases that filter. Allowing the same ≥0.80 late-favorite price rule from 70s left (instead of 50s) aims to lift an ask before the late book goes one-sided. A 1-minute backtest of slightly earlier late entries stayed strongly positive; a looser 120s-left proxy was still positive but weaker, so the late gate stops at 70s. Hard stop and sizing are unchanged. A’s own 50s late-favorite rule is unchanged."},{"time_pt":"6:36 PM PT Nov 10","account":"M5","old":"T’s 60–150s / 45–60¢ rule, plus 3 consecutive polls where book imbalance I is strictly on the same side (I>0 for UP, I<0 for DOWN), $5","new":"Same T entry rule, plus 2 consecutive polls where I > −0.25 for UP or I < +0.25 for DOWN, $5","reason":"Zero trades in ~26 hours even though T filled three times in that span. On all three of those T fills, top-of-book imbalance I was on the opposite side (or nearly flat), so a strict same-side I>0 / I<0 filter could never agree. Lowered the agreement floor from 0 to −0.25 / +0.25 and required 2 agreeing snapshots instead of 3. That would have allowed 2 of T’s 3 live trades (the UP fill at I=−0.25 would still be blocked). Expected rate approaches T’s when the book is not strongly opposed (T’s 18-day backtest is ~10 trades/day / +$115 at $5; live T has been quieter)."}],"coinbase_lag":{"reachable":true,"samples":900,"last_price":62741.57,"last_diff_bp":-8.0361,"mean_abs_bp":3.4263},"btc_minutes":{"as_of":"6:29:05 PM PT","source":"BRTI","last":62742.28,"series":[{"ts":1795051800,"t":"5:30 PM","c":62563.37,"d":-39.25,"dir":"down"},{"ts":1795051860,"t":"5:31 PM","c":62505.09,"d":-58.28,"dir":"down"},{"ts":1795051920,"t":"5:32 PM","c":62464.22,"d":-40.87,"dir":"down"},{"ts":1795051980,"t":"5:33 PM","c":62429.96,"d":-34.26,"dir":"down"},{"ts":1795052040,"t":"5:34 PM","c":62372.28,"d":-57.68,"dir":"down"},{"ts":1795052100,"t":"5:35 PM","c":62354.11,"d":-18.17,"dir":"down"},{"ts":1795052160,"t":"5:36 PM","c":62438.89,"d":84.78,"dir":"up"},{"ts":1795052220,"t":"5:37 PM","c":62425.62,"d":-13.27,"dir":"down"},{"ts":1795052280,"t":"5:38 PM","c":62384.72,"d":-40.9,"dir":"down"},{"ts":1795052340,"t":"5:39 PM","c":62544.83,"d":160.11,"dir":"up"},{"ts":1795052400,"t":"5:40 PM","c":62556.86,"d":12.03,"dir":"up"},{"ts":1795052460,"t":"5:41 PM","c":62670.4,"d":113.54,"dir":"up"},{"ts":1795052520,"t":"5:42 PM","c":62727.71,"d":57.31,"dir":"up"},{"ts":1795052580,"t":"5:43 PM","c":62730.68,"d":2.97,"dir":"up"},{"ts":1795052640,"t":"5:44 PM","c":62725.26,"d":-5.42,"dir":"down"},{"ts":1795052700,"t":"5:45 PM","c":62709.7,"d":-15.56,"dir":"down"},{"ts":1795052760,"t":"5:46 PM","c":62630.98,"d":-78.72,"dir":"down"},{"ts":1795052820,"t":"5:47 PM","c":62670.91,"d":39.93,"dir":"up"},{"ts":1795052880,"t":"5:48 PM","c":62664.23,"d":-6.68,"dir":"down"},{"ts":1795052940,"t":"5:49 PM